{# The known-library match section, shared by every engine template that #}
{# feeds the library-match findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading #}
{# text, scan coverage record) so each template passes its own heading text #}
{# and the coverage the producing scan stamped. The body is #}
{# verbatim-pinned by the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting #}
{# drift fails CI. #}
{# Each match record carries its own version-authority note (issue #347): #}
{# the signature matched some release, which release is not established. The #}
{# note rides the record — an admitted finding renders one extra "Admission:" #}
{# line beside its Evidence; a finding with no note renders what it rendered #}
{# before. #}
{# The coverage record (issue #347) arrives as CoverageInfo strings: the #}
{# scan's status word and its admission line. The include appends exactly #}
{# one "Coverage:" qualification line — beside the entries, or as the whole #}
{# section beside the heading when the scan stamped no findings but admits #}
{# falling short — whenever the record carries an admission; a complete or #}
{# missing record renders exactly what it rendered before. #}
{% macro libmatch_section(findings, heading, coverage) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The functions this one calls that static analysis has identified as
statically linked known-library code — the C runtime or the C++ standard
library. Do NOT re-implement these bodies: map each call onto the
suggested Rust equivalent instead:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** — `{{ finding.function }}` matches `{{ finding.symbol }}` ({{ finding.family }} library, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% if !finding.admission.is_empty() %}  Admission: {{ finding.admission }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
